 ],
 "caption": "Nobody drew this identity. Sound made it.\n\nApple Music introduced its new visual identity on 21 October. According to AppleInsider, the logo was etched into the glass floor of a small tank of mineral oil, a transducer played a few chosen notes until the liquid rippled, and the whole thing was filmed in camera, with no CGI. Fred again.. worked on the notes with NEST Acoustics, and those notes became the brand's sonic signature. MacRumors reports the colour moved from red to black and white.\n\nMy take: the lesson for any small brand is to pull the identity out of what you actually make, not out of decoration.\n\nThe limits: it's too early to say whether people like it or whether it works for the brand; no results have been published. Process details come from press coverage, not an official Apple page, and MacRumors says water where AppleInsider says mineral oil.\n\nWhat sound, smell or trace does your work have that your identity still ignores? Write to me.\n\n— Behnood Kavian",
